  "question": {
    "text": "An unbiased coin is tossed <math><mn>5</mn></math> times. Suppose that a variable <math><mi>X</mi></math> is assigned the value <math><mi>k</mi></math> when <math><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;consecutive heads are obtained for <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> otherwise <math><mi>X</mi></math> takes the value <math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then the expected value of <math><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zJJ89",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
